<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>DataIntake - sample audits</title>
<style>
  :root { --bg: #fbfaf8; --panel: #fff; --text: #1d1d1f; --muted: #6b6b70; --line: #e6e3de;
    --critical: #b42318; --warning: #9a6700; --accent: #2e5e4e; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg: #141415; --panel: #1c1c1e; --text: #ececed; --muted: #a0a0a6; --line: #2e2e31;
      --critical: #ff8a80; --warning: #f5c451; --accent: #8fd1b5; }
  }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text);
    font: 15px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 20px 80px; }
  h1 { font-size: 30px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  p.lead { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 32px; font-size: 16px; }
  .card { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 22px; margin: 16px 0; }
  .card h2 { font-size: 19px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .counts { margin: 12px 0; display: flex; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 14px; }
  .counts b { font-size: 20px; margin-right: 4px; }
  .critical b { color: var(--critical); } .warning b { color: var(--warning); }
  a.button { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg); text-decoration: none;
    padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; margin-right: 10px; }
  .files { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 13px; }
  .files a { color: var(--accent); margin-right: 10px; }
  footer { margin-top: 48px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>DataIntake</h1>
  <p class="lead">A first-day audit of whatever data a client sends: what each file holds, what is wrong
    with it in plain language, how the files connect, and which metrics it can support. Below are
    audits of two sample businesses whose exports were made messy on purpose.</p>
  {% for c in cards %}
  <div class="card">
    <h2>{{ c.name }}</h2>
    <div class="muted">{{ c.blurb }}</div>
    <div class="counts">
      <span class="critical"><b>{{ c.audit.count("critical") }}</b>critical</span>
      <span class="warning"><b>{{ c.audit.count("warning") }}</b>warnings</span>
      <span><b>{{ c.audit.kpis | length }}</b>supported metrics</span>
    </div>
    <a class="button" href="{{ c.key }}/">Open the audit</a>
    <div class="files muted">Raw exports:
      {% for f in c.files %}<a href="exports/{{ c.key }}/{{ f }}">{{ f }}</a>{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <footer>Sample data is synthetic. Source and method: github.com/m4dd0ck/data-intake</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
